<block xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd"
  xmlns:btype="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core">
  <name>Text</name>
  <type>btype:Text</type>
  <baseType>btype:PrimitiveType</baseType>
  <idea>Primitive BlockML type for textual values — implementation-independent.</idea>

  <documentation>BOM Core primitive ValueType for text. Unqualified name Text resolves to
    org.blockml.bml.type.Text. Replaces the former String type — BlockML describes semantic types, not
    implementation data structures. Renderers may map Text to Java String, TypeScript string,
    Python str, C# string, or any target representation.

    Semantic subtypes extend Text: FullyQualifiedName, Version, URL, URI, FilePath, MimeType, …
    Concrete payload values are stored on Properties — not on the Text type itself.

    Optional configuration Properties (minLength, maxLength) configure a Property's owned Text
    instance via inline type syntax — Text{maxLength=100}. Positional order: minLength, maxLength.
    See 20_value_type_instance_configuration.md.</documentation>
  <properties>
    <minLength type="Integer">
      <documentation>Minimum allowed text length (inclusive). Configured via Text{minLength=n}.</documentation>
    </minLength>
    <maxLength type="Integer">
      <documentation>Maximum allowed text length (inclusive). Configured via Text{maxLength=n}.</documentation>
    </maxLength>
  </properties>
</block>
